# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore to decide
# what goes in the upload tarball — so it has to repeat the ordinary excludes
# (node_modules, build output) as well as the project-specific ones.
#
# Without this, the archive came to 423 MB and the upload died with ECONNRESET
# partway through. The mobile app itself is only a few MB; the bulk is ML
# datasets, the separately-deployed backend, and local documentation.

# ── deps & build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.gradle/

# ── native dirs: EAS runs its own prebuild, so don't ship local ones ─────────
android/
ios/

# ── ML datasets & model artifacts (hundreds of MB, unused by the app build) ──
data/
plantDetection/
images/

# ── backend: deployed separately on Render, not part of the mobile build ─────
backend/

# ── local docs, reports and scratch files (root level only) ──────────────────
important-tips/
docs/
/*.html
/*.docx
/*.doc
/*.xlsx
/*.md
/*.py
*.zip
*.rar
*.pdf

# ── vcs & temp ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
tmp/
rohit_code/
rishab code/
